          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "રોપવું — ropvũ — \"to plant, to set out\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "તેણે બગીચામાં છોડ રોપ્યો. — teṇe bagīcāmā̃ choḍ ropyo — \"She planted a plant in the garden.\""
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "વાવવું is to sow seed; રોપવું (ropvũ) is to put a young plant in the ground."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "રોપવું (ropvũ) is a tadbhava. CDIAL lists it, glossed \"to plant\", under ropyate, \"is planted\", the passive of Sanskrit ropayati, \"plants\", in its entry for rupati, \"pierces, makes a hole, plants\" (CDIAL 10783)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
